@startuml arch-authpolicy-jwt
!define RECTANGLE class

skinparam component {
  BackgroundColor<<browser>> LightBlue
  BackgroundColor<<gateway>> LightGreen
  BackgroundColor<<policy>> Pink
  BackgroundColor<<backend>> LightGray
  BackgroundColor<<keycloak>> Yellow
  BorderColor Black
  ArrowColor Black
}

skinparam defaultTextAlignment center

title AuthPolicy (JWT) Architecture\n(Keycloak JWT Token Validation)

rectangle "Browser\n(UI)" as browser <<browser>>
rectangle "AWS Load Balancer\n+ OpenShift Router" as router <<gateway>>
rectangle "Keycloak\nToken Issuer\n- Issues JWT tokens\n- JWKS endpoint" as keycloak <<keycloak>>
rectangle "Gateway\nrhcl-workshop-gw\n- TLS termination" as gateway <<gateway>>
rectangle "HTTPRoute\njwt-protected-api\n- Path: /protected" as httproute <<gateway>>
rectangle "AuthPolicy (Route-level)\n- JWT validation\n- Issuer: Keycloak\n- JWKS signature verification" as authpolicy <<policy>>
rectangle "Backend Service\nprotected-api\n- Pod\n- No auth logic required" as backend <<backend>>

browser -down-> keycloak : "①Token Request\nPOST /token\n(credentials)"
keycloak -up-> browser : "②JWT Token\n(ID token + access token)"

browser -down-> router : "③API Request\nGET /protected\nAuthorization: Bearer <JWT>"
router -down-> gateway : "SNI routing"
gateway -down-> httproute : "Route match"
httproute -down-> keycloak : "④JWT validation\nVerify signature with JWKS"
keycloak -up-> httproute : "⑤Signature valid"
httproute -down-> backend : "⑥Forward\n(JWT validated)"

authpolicy -right-> httproute : "applies to\n(JWT validation)"

note right of authpolicy
**JWT Validation Steps**
①Extract token from Authorization header
②Verify signature with Keycloak JWKS
③Check expiration (exp claim)
④Check issuer (iss claim)
⑤Check audience (aud claim)

**Results:**
• Valid token → allow
• Missing/invalid/expired → 401
end note

note right of backend
**Backend Benefits**
- No authentication logic required
- Trusts Gateway validation
- Can optionally extract JWT claims
  (Gateway forwards token in header)
- Focus on business logic only
end note

note left of browser
**UI Features**
- Get token from Keycloak
- Decode JWT (display claims)
- Call API without token → 401
- Call API with token → 200
end note

@enduml
